<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - May 21.</title>
<headline>S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - May 21.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the arrival schedule for major steel scrap vessels unloading at South Korean ports of Inchon, Pusan, Masan, Pohang, Kwangyang and Asan, as detailed on Wednesday by South Korean surveyors.</p>
<p>Steel scrap cargoes</p>
<p>-- INCHON PORT</p>
<p> VESSEL	    TONNE    ETA	 ETD	  BUYER</p>
<p> Jade Orient     30,000   May 20    May 26     Inchon</p>
<p> Grande	    45,000   May 25    Jun  5     Inchon</p>
<p> Rova		38,391   Jun 20		   Inchon</p>
<p>-- PUSAN PORT </p>
<p> Delta-Trident   35,000   Jun 10		   Dongkuk</p>
<p>-- MASAN PORT</p>
<p> Venus	     39,185   Jun 14		   Kisco</p>
<p>-- POHANG PORT</p>
<p> Thornhill	 35,512   May 20    Jun  9     Kangwon</p>
<p> Nurten Ana	33,000   May 25    Jun 13     Kangwon</p>
<p> T.B.N.	    25,000   End of May	    POSCO</p>
<p>-- KWANGYANG PORT</p>
<p> Western Friend  36,500   May 11    May 24     POSCO</p>
<p> Aspidoforos     30,500   May 24		   POSCO</p>
<p> Feng Yan	  50,000   End of June	    POSCO</p>
<p> Caspian Trident 35,000   End of June	    POSCO</p>
<p>-- ASAN PORT</p>
<p> Pisces Pioneer  28,361   May 14    May 25     Hanbo</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5650</p>
